# ======================================================================
# checkCIF Alert Rule Definitions
# Derived from PLATON validation checks (A.L. Spek, Utrecht University)
# ======================================================================
#
# FORMAT
# ------
# Non-comment, non-blank lines contain colon-delimited fields:
#
#   CODE : TYPE : SEVERITY : DESCRIPTION
#
# CODE        3-digit zero-padded alert identifier
# TYPE        1 = composition/general   2 = ADP/thermal
# SEVERITY    Single letter (A, B, or C) for fixed-level presence checks
#             Three slash-separated values (C/B/A ascending thresholds) for
#             value-based graded checks.  The diagnostic value is compared
#             against these limits in descending severity order.
# DESCRIPTION Human-readable alert text.  Placeholders:
#             $F = floating-point diagnostic value
#             $I = integer diagnostic value
#             $A = atom label or string identifier
#
# ======================================================================

040 : 1 : C : No H-atoms in this Carbon Containing Compound .. $A Please Check
041 : 1 : C : Calc. and Reported SumFormula Strings Differ .. $A Please Check
043 : 1 : 0.1/1.0/10.0 : Calculated and Reported Mol. Weight Differ by .. $F %
044 : 1 : 1.0/5.0/10.0 : Calculated and Reported Density Dx Differ by .. $F %
046 : 1 : 1.0/5.0/10.0 : Reported Z, MW and D(calc) are Inconsistent .... $F %
049 : 1 : C : Calculated Density Less Than 1.0 gcm-3 ......... $F Check
060 : 1 : C : Unknown CIF Data Item(s) Not in Dictionary ...... $I Report
201 : 2 : 0/10/999 : Non-H Atoms with Isotropic ADPs .............. $I Report
211 : 2 : B : Non-Positive Definite ADP Tensor .................. $A Check
213 : 2 : 3.0/4.0/5.0 : ADP Eigenvalue Ratio sqrt(Umax/Umin) ......... $F Check
224 : 1 : 0.002/0.003/0.005 : Ueq(obs) and Ueq(calc) Differ by ............. $F Ang**2
